course: dictionary
lesson: 644
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. Bacon is a food, but it is also part of two idioms, which are phrases whose meaning is not the same as the words in them. Look at the sentence around the word to find which meaning fits.
explain: «Ham, bacon and sausages come from pigs.» Here bacon means the salty meat from a pig. You can ask: could I eat it for breakfast? Yes, so this is the food meaning.
explain: Idioms are about what people mean, not what the words say. If someone says they will bring home the bacon, nobody is carrying pork through the door. It means they will earn money for their family. Try the meaning in the sentence and check that it still makes sense.
fact: Bacon is salty meat from the back or sides of a pig, cut in thin slices.
fact: Bacon is usually fried or grilled before it is eaten.
fact: «To bring home the bacon» means to earn money for your family.
fact: «To save someone's bacon» means to rescue them from trouble.
fact: Bacon is uncountable, so you say some bacon, not two bacons.
exercise: «Ham, bacon and sausages come from pigs.» Which animal do they come from? | A sheep | *A pig | A hen | A cow
exercise: Dad says, «I work hard to bring home the bacon.» What does he mean? | *He earns money for his family | He keeps pigs on a farm | He cooks bacon every day | He saves people from trouble
exercise: «Lunch was bacon and broad beans, and a macaroni pudding.» What else was on the lunch menu besides bacon and broad beans? | A bowl of soup | *A macaroni pudding | A boiled egg | A cup of tea
test: Ellie lost her bag, but her brother found it and saved her bacon. What does «saved her bacon» mean? | *Rescued her from trouble | Gave her a bag of money | Hid her bag in a box | Ate her breakfast with her
test: «Some families eat no pork for religious reasons.» Why might a family not eat bacon? | Bacon is a kind of fruit | Bacon is too expensive | *Their religion means they do not eat pork | Bacon makes you sleepy
exam: Which meaning does bacon have in «Milk from a cow, an egg from a hen, maybe bacon from a pig»? | *Salty meat from a pig, cut in thin slices | A famous English thinker | To rescue someone from trouble | To earn money for your family
